          "end": 1327
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "3. Although the mediation report annexed to the record would show that the mediation has failed, it is submitted by the learned counsel for the informant and the petitioner that earlier also a mediation proceeding was there pursuant to which the husband had taken his wife along with him.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1329,
      "end": 1618,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "However,\nthe Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.70226 of 2024(5) dt.10-04-2025 records would reveal that no such report is annexed to the present application.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1619,
      "end": 1772,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Patna High Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 1632,
          "end": 1648
        },
        {
          "text": "CR. MISC. No.70226 of 2024(5)",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 1649,
          "end": 1678
        },
        {
          "text": "dt.10-04-2025",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1679,
          "end": 1692
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "Call for a report from the Mediation Centre, Patna High Court, Patna with reference to earlier mediation proceeding as a the result of which, the petitioner had taken his wife along with him.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1774,
      "end": 1965,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Patna High Court, Patna",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 1819,
          "end": 1842
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "Learned counsel for the informant, however, makes a submission that the informant is not safe in the house of the petitioner which is opposed by the learned counsel for the petitioner, who says that the informant is being kept in her matrimonial house with all dignity and honour.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1966,
      "end": 2247,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
